with Bridge we can build simple but yet flexible hierarchy!
we use "POLYMORPHISM" to divide our multi dimensional hierarchy to one dimension.
we use bridge pattern when we have a hierarchy that can grow in two different dimensions.
we can split the complex hierarchy to some simple separated ones!

indeed we convert one inheritance to "COMPOSITION",
this composition (like device field) is our bridge,
we create two separate hierarchy that connect to each other by this bridge
(each new hierarchy is one dimensional)

Note: we have feature hierarchy &
      Implementation (device) hierarchy in our example.

Note: we can now add new brand like LG, just by one new class
      we can now add new feature like nextChannel(), just by add new method on AdvancedRemoteControl:             public void nextChannel() {
                                                                                                                        device.setChannel(device.getChannel() + 1);
                                                                                                                       }


